%N A398470 Number of increasing 3-term arithmetic progressions in an n^3 cube.
%C A398470 Each term in the arithmetic progression is a 3-dimensional coordinate vector. One coordinate vector is considered to be greater than another if each of its coordinate values is at least as large and they are not all equal.
%H A398470 Hiller Alves Fernandes, <a href="https://zenodo.org/records/21708794">Counting 3-Term Arithmetic Progressions in Integer Hypercubes</a>, Zenodo (2026).
%F A398470 For n even: a(n) = (n^6-8*n^3)/16.
%F A398470 For n odd: a(n) = ((n^2+1)^3-8*n^3)/16.
%o A398470 (Python)
%o A398470 def a(n):
%o A398470     return (n**6 - 8*n**3) // 16 if n % 2 == 0 else ((n**2 + 1)**3 - 8*n**3) // 16
%o A398470 terms = [a(n) for n in range(1, 36)]
%o A398470 print(terms)
%Y A398470 Column 3 of A397600.
